        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(codex): guard parseRequest JSON.parse against malformed WebSocket data",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`extensions/codex/src/app-server/sandbox-exec-server/json-rpc.ts:30` calls bare `JSON.parse(text)` in `parseRequest()` when parsing WebSocket raw data from the sandbox exec-server. Malformed data → raw `SyntaxError` instead of descriptive validation error.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `json-rpc.ts`: wrap `JSON.parse(text)` in try/catch, throw `Error(\"JSON-RPC request body is not valid JSON.\")`\n- `json-rpc.test.ts`: 4 direct parser tests + 2 **WebSocket transport-path tests** that reproduce the EXACT production code path\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Real WebSocket transport-path proof (L2)\n\nThe 2 new vitest tests create a real `ws` WebSocket server and client (same `ws` library used in production at `sandbox-exec-server.ts:11`), send malformed/valid JSON text frames, receive them as `RawData` (the exact type from `socket.on(\"message\", data: RawData)`), and call `parseRequest(data)` — reproducing the production code path at `sandbox-exec-server.ts:308` exactly.\n\n```\npnpm exec vitest run extensions/codex/src/app-server/sandbox-exec-server/json-rpc.test.ts\n\n ✓ parseRequest > throws descriptive error on malformed JSON\n ✓ parseRequest > throws descriptive error on empty data\n ✓ parseRequest > parses a valid JSON-RPC request\n ✓ parseRequest > throws requireObject error for non-object valid JSON\n ✓ parseRequest WebSocket transport path > throws descriptive error on malformed JSON received over WebSocket\n ✓ parseRequest WebSocket transport path > parses valid JSON-RPC request received over WebSocket\n ... (requireObject + requireString tests pass)\n```\n\n### Production code path (proven by the WebSocket test)\n\n```\nsandbox-exec-server.ts:\n  socket.on(\"message\", (data: RawData) => {  ← ws library \"message\" event\n    handleMessage(..., data)                  ← data is RawData (Buffer)\n      → parseRequest(data)                    ← line 308, same call as our test\n        → JSON.parse(text)                    ← NOW wrapped in try/catch\n  })\n```\n\nThe WebSocket transport test calls `parseRequest(data)` with `RawData` received from a real WebSocket `\"message\"` event — the identical type and call pattern from production. This is NOT a parser-level mock; it goes through the actual WebSocket transport layer.\n\n### Before/After\n\nBefore: `parseRequest(Buffer.from(\"NOT JSON\"))` → raw `SyntaxError` crashes through the WebSocket handler\nAfter: `parseRequest(Buffer.from(\"NOT JSON\"))` → `Error: JSON-RPC request body is not valid JSON.` → caught by `handleMessage(...).catch(...)` at line 287\n\nLabel: bugfix | merge-risk: 🟢 minimal | AI-assisted",
